{"name":"Happy Skeleton","hex":"#faeed7","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"happy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a feeling arising from a consciousness of well-being or of enjoyment; enjoying good of any kind, such as comfort, peace, or tranquillity; blissful, contented, joyous.","Experiencing the effect of favourable fortune; favored by fortune or luck; fortunate, lucky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A happy event, thing, person, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happy"},{"term":"skeleton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The system that provides support to an organism, where in vertebrates it is internal and consists of bones and cartilage, and external in some other animals.","An anthropomorphic representation of a skeleton."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reduce to a skeleton; to skin; to skeletonize.","To minimize."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skeleton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skeleton","blocks":[{"text":"A skeleton is the structural frame that supports the body of most animals. There are several types of skeletons, including the exoskeleton, which is a rigid outer shell that holds up an organism's shape; the endoskeleton, a rigid internal frame to which the organs and soft tissues attach; and the hydroskeleton, a flexible internal structure supported by the hydrostatic pressure of body fluids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Horse_and_Man.jpg/330px-Horse_and_Man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeleton","wikidata":"Q7881"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Horse_and_Man.jpg/500px-Horse_and_Man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Horse_and_Man.jpg/500px-Horse_and_Man.jpg?utm_source=en.wi